      "content": "To systematically investigate these small discrepancies, start by segmenting the transactions based on the petty cash codes and the frequency of the variances. Then, cross-reference these outliers against purchase order logs and vendor receipts to see if there are supporting documentation gaps. Finally, conduct focused, brief interviews with the personnel responsible for petty cash management to understand the workflow for those specific transactions. This targeted approach can uncover procedural weaknesses without necessitating a full audit.",
